        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nevin McCaskill, Merv Krakau\n- Organizations: Buffalo Bills, New England Patriots, New York Giants, New York Jets, NFL\n- Places: New York, East Rutherford, New Jersey, Jefferson, Iowa, MetLife Stadium\n- Roles: undrafted free agent, linebacker, professional American football player\n\nFacts:\n- Mervin Floyd Krakau was born on May 16, 1951, in Jefferson, Iowa.\n- Merv Krakau is a former professional American football player who played linebacker for six seasons for the Buffalo Bills and the New England Patriots.\n- Nevin McCaskill was signed by the Buffalo Bills as an undrafted free agent in 2007.\n- The Buffalo Bills are the only NFL team that plays its home games in the state of New York.\n- The New York Giants and New York Jets play at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, New Jersey, rather than in New York state.",
